wb-docker-app (0.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Minimal-first cut (docs/adr/0003): the helper is now a thin lifecycle glue
    over curated, static services. Removed:
    - wb-diag-collect integration (collector script + diag drop-in);
    - the runtime port allocator, the nginx renderer and the app descriptor;
    - the day-2 sugar verbs (status/logs/restart/update/list) — use systemctl
      and docker directly.
  * Services are now static: each ships its own base compose with a fixed
    loopback port and its own static nginx drop-in, so the helper neither reads
    compose labels nor renders nginx at runtime. New tolerant `reload-proxy`
    verb reloads nginx from a service's postrm after the drop-in is removed.
  * `install` now also refreshes package-owned code (e.g. a service's vendored
    Node-RED palette under <app>/palette/) into the user's data layer,
    overwriting our own subtree on upgrade while leaving user files alone
    (docs/adr/0006).
  * `install` enables a service's nginx site itself (absolute-target symlink into
    sites-enabled) and accepts --data-uid to chown the seeded data dir to a
    non-root container user. Both fix controller-validated bugs: a relative
    dh_link symlink breaks on WB's bind-mounted sites-enabled, and a root-owned
    /data blocks a uid-1000 container. Build-Depends now needs
    pybuild-plugin-pyproject.
  * `install` now restarts the systemd instance (enable + restart, not
    enable --now) so an upgraded image tag is actually applied — the running
    container is recreated on the current compose instead of staying on the old
    image until a reboot.
  * MQTT boot-timing (docs/adr/0004): mosquitto keeps its early boot via the
    net.ipv4.ip_nonlocal_bind sysctl instead of an After=docker.service
    ordering; the provision writes a marker only after a successful restart so a
    failed restart is retried. The helper no longer provisions MQTT at its own
    install — provisioning is now lazy, triggered by the first bridge-service
    that needs the broker (idempotent singleton).

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0300

wb-docker-app (0.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging tails for day-2 lifecycle & observability (issue #5):
    - apt.conf.d drop-in excluding wb-docker-app and wb-* service packages
      from unattended-upgrades (upgrades stay explicit);
    - wb-diag-collect drop-in + collector script capturing each service's
      systemctl status and recent journal logs into the diagnostic archive;
    - documented downgrade/rollback (apt downgrade) and the pre-major-upgrade
      data-backup warning (design.md §3.11.1).

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Tue, 02 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

wb-docker-app (0.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: templated systemd unit wb-docker-app@.service, the
    wb-docker-app Python CLI, and the shell library (issue #1, walking
    skeleton).

